# Coding standards — pointer

Authoritative source: `docs/RULES.md` (Coding Standards, Testing Rules,
Security Rules, Git & Documentation). Read it before editing.

Key anchors (verify against RULES.md, do not rely on memory):

- Type hints on every function; Pydantic v2 at all seams; no untyped dicts
  as Mandates.
- Deep services, small public interfaces; inject `db_path` and Razorpay
  clients — never construct SQLite or Razorpay inside parser/policy/firewall.
- Parser checks structure; Vault checks identity/TTL/revocation/denylist;
  Guardrails come later.
- Money actions gated: no Razorpay call unless Firewall + parser + Vault +
  Guardrails all pass.
- Every terminal path (allow or Refusal) writes an Audit event.
- Refusal with `reason_code` is a coded success outcome, not a bare exception.
- Unit tests hit service public interfaces only. `pytest tests/unit -q`
  green at the end of each phase.
- Vocabulary from `docs/CONTEXT.md` in types, tests, and issue titles.
